// ULTRAKILL TAS - minimal TAS baking example.
//
// The ticks between bake_start and bake_end form one bake block. The first run records
// the world state at the end of every tick into "bake_block_example-room1.ukbake" next to
// this file. Later runs use it when the General tab's Baking card says so:
//   Enable Baked Playback      inputs still run, then the baked state is applied each tick
//   Verify Raw Playback        pure live playback, first drift per block is reported
//   Skip Baked Blocks to End   jump to the block's last baked frame, continue live after it
// Any edit to the header or to a line before bake_end changes the block's checksum, and the
// block is recorded again on the next run. For a block that should leave doors and streamed
// map rooms live instead of baking them, use bake_start_nme in place of bake_start.
version 1
host_frametime 0.008
seed 1337
start_type restart_mission
frames
// settle on the ground
----------|------|------|-|90.0|0.0|20|
bake_start room1
// run forward, jump, keep running
----------|f-----|------|-|90.0|0.0|40|
----------|f-----|j-----|-|-|-|1|
----------|f-----|------|-|-|-|60|
bake_end
// live again after the block
----------|------|------|-|-|-|20|
